+## Steps
+
+### Tier A — free smoke on your workspace (read-only)
+
+#### Step 1 — The gate: the real env file and its policy lines `[FREE]`
+
+**Do:**
+
+```bash
+F=/etc/aidev02/aienv.d/defaults.sh
+ls -l "$F"
+[ -w "$F" ] && echo "WRITABLE by $(id -un)" || echo "not writable by $(id -un)"
+grep -n -E 'CCSESSION_.*(TIER_RULES|ACCESS)|CCSESSION_DEFAULT_TIER|CCSESSION_MODEL_ORDER' "$F"
+grep -c -E '^[[:space:]]*export[[:space:]]+T[0-9]{1,2}[a-z]?_WINDOW=' "$F"
+```
+
+**Expected result:**
+
+- `ls` lists the file; `not writable by <you>`. The file is pushed from the Coder template and changed only through review (`README.md:276,352-354`). UNVERIFIED: its owner and mode are set by the Coder template, outside this repo; on the workspace where this guide was written they were `-rw-r--r-- root root`. `WRITABLE` is a finding for the Coder admin: any workspace user could then change everyone's policy.
+- Each of `CCSESSION_TIER_RULES` and `CCSESSION_ACCESS` appears on at most one line, as one `export NAME="..."` (or the guarded `[ -z "${NAME:-}" ] && export NAME=...` form), and nowhere else, comments included (`models.py:95-103,416-433`; `README.md:332-336`). A second line naming either one is a FAIL of the real file: it stops ccsession for every Coder user.
+- A count of 1 or more: tier mode is on (`models.py:469-479`). `0`: tier mode is off in this workspace; Tier A Step 2 and Tier C do not apply (mark them N/A).
+
+**Pass/Fail:** ☐ PASS ☐ FAIL — notes: `______`
+
+#### Step 2 — Your own access as ccsession sees it `[FREE]`
+
+**Do:**
+
+```bash
+echo "owner=${CODER_WORKSPACE_OWNER_NAME:-<unset>} roles=${CODER_WORKSPACE_OWNER_ROLES:-<unset>}"
+ccsession --models-status | tail -n 2
+ccsession --help | sed -n '/^Tiers in this workspace/,$p'
+```
+
+**Expected result:**
+
+- Your Coder username and comma-separated roles. A plain member holds `member` (Coder also sends `organization-member`); site-wide roles such as `owner`, `user-admin`, `template-admin`, `auditor` appear when you hold them (`models.py:509-519`; `README.md:318-320`).
+- `Tier mode:          on (settings from /etc/aidev02/aienv.d/defaults.sh); tiers: <every defined tier>`, then an `Access:` line (`models.py:1004-1025`; `ccsession:1432-1435`), one of:
+  - `Access:             <you> starts on <tier>; tiers: <your tiers>[; models listed] (CCSESSION_TIER_RULES[, <role:... or *>])` when an entry applies to you; the part after the comma names the role or `*` entry that matched, and is absent for a username entry (`models.py:611-618,1014-1020`).
+  - `Access:             <you>: not listed; default tier, every tier` when none does (`models.py:1021-1025`).
+  - `Tier mode:          on (...); tiers: invalid (<reason>)` when the file is broken for you: a FAIL of the real file (`models.py:1008-1013`).
+- The help ends with `Tiers in this workspace (* = default):` and one `ccsession --tier <tier>` entry per tier on your `Access:` line, with `*` on your start tier (`ccsession:1402-1413`; `models.py:923-935`).
+
+**Pass/Fail:** ☐ PASS ☐ FAIL ☐ N/A — notes: `______`
