+#### Step 7 — A broken or duplicate entry stops the launch with the reason `[LOCAL-WRITE]`
+
+**Do:** each `ccsession e01-check` line is a launch the policy must refuse; each `default-tier` line is what a launch runs for another user (`ccsession:954`):
+
+```bash
+rule dup 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="alice=tier2 alice=tier3 *=tier2"'
+rule undef 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="alice=tier9 *=tier2"'
+rule startout 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="alice=tier1a:tier2,tier3"'
+rule emptylist 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="alice=tier2:"'
+rule stray 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="alice=tier2 :tier3 *=tier2"'
+rule twostar 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="*=tier2:tier2 *=tier3"'
+rule comment 'export CCSESSION_TIER_RULES="alice=tier2"' '# CCSESSION_TIER_RULES was tier3 before'
+for f in dup undef startout emptylist stray comment; do
+  e1 AIDEV_AI_DEFAULTS_PATH=/tmp/e01/$f.sh CODER_WORKSPACE_OWNER_NAME=alice ccsession e01-check; echo "$f alice exit=$?"
+done
+for f in dup undef stray comment; do
+  e1 AIDEV_AI_DEFAULTS_PATH=/tmp/e01/$f.sh CODER_WORKSPACE_OWNER_NAME=bob python3 "$E1_MODELS" default-tier; echo "$f bob exit=$?"
+done
+e1 AIDEV_AI_DEFAULTS_PATH=/tmp/e01/twostar.sh ccsession e01-check; echo "twostar no-owner exit=$?"
+```
+
